According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global LED bulb market was valued at USD 28.5 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 56.2 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 7 % during the forecast period (2025–2034). This growth is propelled by tightening energy efficiency standards worldwide, declining component costs, and a rising consumer preference for smart connected lighting solutions.
LED bulbs are solid state lighting devices that generate illumination through semiconductor diodes rather than filaments or gas discharge tubes. Because they convert a higher proportion of electrical energy into visible light, they consume up to 80 % less power than traditional incandescent lamps while delivering comparable brightness and longer service life.
